## Why This Is Asked

This question probes how a candidate designs a privacy-conscious, multi-tenant ML pipeline on GCP, balancing data governance, per-tenant isolation, cost, and operability.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation with per-tenant datasets and Feature Store
- PII de-identification in Dataflow
- Canary deployments and traffic shifting
- Drift detection and Explainable AI for governance
- Privacy logging and rollback mechanisms

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: shift partial traffic to canary on drift alert
function rollbackOnDrift(isDrift, canaryEndpoint, prodEndpoint){
  if(!isDrift) return;
  // gradually shift traffic back to prod
  setTraffic(canaryEndpoint, 0.0);
  setTraffic(prodEndpoint, 1.0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding with data retention?
- How would you scale feature store lookups for thousands of tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a candidate's ability to design a compliant, language-agnostic text classification pipeline using Vertex AI, Dataflow, and Pub/Sub, with privacy safeguards and practical operational concerns.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow-based redaction and translation for multilingual content
- End-to-end data lineage: storage of raw and processed text
- Weekly Vertex AI training with canary deployment
- Drift and latency monitoring with rollback strategy
- Practical cost considerations: storage, translation, training, and serving

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: dataflow-style transform for redaction/translation
function redactAndTranslate(record) {
  const redacted = redactPII(record.text);
  const translated = (record.language !== 'en') ? translate(redacted, 'en') : redacted;
  return { id: record.id, text_en: translated, raw: record.text };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate translation quality across languages in this setup?
- What changes would you make to handle sudden traffic spikes without violating privacy constraints?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving ML at scale with regulatory constraints, multi-tenant isolation, and production-grade governance. Requires knowledge of Vertex AI Confidential Computing, Dataflow pipelines, Data Catalog/DLP, and automated rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI Confidential Computing (VMs/TPUs)
- Dataflow ingestion and residency controls
- Private endpoints and per-tenant budgets
- Data Catalog governance and DLP coverage
- Adversarial robustness testing and dataset/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: basic adversarial test harness
function evalAdversarial(model, sample) {
  const adv = generateAdversarialSample(sample);
  const pred = model.predict(adv);
  return pred.accuracy;
}
```

